### Procurement API - HTTP requests for manual testing
# Replace placeholders like {{mrId}} and {{prId}} with real IDs returned by the API.

### Create Material Requisition
POST http://localhost:3000/api/procurement/mr
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "department": "IT",
  "requestedBy": "alice@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "itemCode": "IT-001",
      "description": "Laptop",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitOfMeasure": "PCS"
    }
  ]
}

### Submit Material Requisition (use returned MR id)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/procurement/mr/{{mrId}}/submit


### Approve Material Requisition (use returned MR id)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/procurement/mr/{{mrId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approvedBy": "manager@example.com"
}


### Get Purchase Request by id (replace {{prId}})
GET http://localhost:3000/api/procurement/pr/{{prId}}


### Approve Purchase Request
POST http://localhost:3000/api/procurement/pr/{{prId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approvedBy": "procurement-manager@example.com"
}


### Notes
# 1) Create MR -> use `mr.id` from response to call submit/approve.
# 2) MR approval triggers PR creation (synchronous domain event) so inspect logs or PR repository to find created PR id.
# 3) If you run the app on a different port or host, update the URLs above.
